.TH SUPIVPN-CLI 8
.SH NAME
supivpn-cli \- local SupiVPN operator frontend
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B supivpn-cli
.RI "command [options]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run with sudo on a combined Debian node/controller host. PostgreSQL may be
external. No remote administration endpoint is provided. Output is bounded JSON.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status [--instance NAME]
Show systemd state of the controller and selected node/OpenVPN pair.
.TP
.B profiles list [--limit 1..100] [--after PROFILE_ID]
List profile records and verified owner_username using an opaque ID cursor.
An empty owner label means unknown. Protect this personal audit data.
.TP
.B profiles status PROFILE_ID
Inspect the verified owner label, state and revision.
.TP
.B profiles block|activate PROFILE_ID --revision N --yes
Change state only if the inspected revision still matches.
.TP
.B sessions status|drop --user NAME [--instance NAME] [--yes]
Inspect or request termination of the exact SAML user on one local listener.
Drop requires --yes. Poll status to confirm closure; it is not a ban.
.SH SECURITY
Requires root, fixed root-owned configuration and a local Unix-connected
node/controller. Profile commands use a restricted transient systemd service.
No secrets are accepted on the command line or returned in output.
Blocking a profile does not disconnect existing tunnels or prevent a newly
issued profile. After a timeout inspect state before retrying a mutation.
.SH FILES
/usr/share/doc/supivpn-cli/CLI.md
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR supivpn (8),
.BR supivpn-controller (8)
